11.text:
The symmetry of the centered Greek cross forces all rows strictly above the horizontal arm to share an identical support pattern with all rows strictly below it. Consequently, exhaustive enumeration of row vectors in any faithful discretization yields exactly two combinatorial classes: the constant vector of all \(a\)s (any row outside canton height or intersecting the horizontal arm) and one shared non-constant pattern (two \(b\)-blocks flanking the vertical red arm, for all rows inside canton height but missing that arm). These two vectors are linearly independent whenever \(a\neq b\), so \(\operatorname{rank}(M)=2\) exactly.

All claims of rank 3 (or higher) arise from either double-counting duplicate patterns or from treating the four white rectangles as independent rank-1 updates; once the vertical arm is taken into account their row supports collapse to a single nonzero direction, confirming that the update contributed by \(W\) is rank at most 1. The decomposition \(M=aJ+(b-a)W\) therefore realizes rank exactly 2 for generic \(a\neq b\).

